**Findings**

- Line 18, selector keyed to unused form: input `[{ name:"A",tE:1,tN:10,cE:2,cN:20,pmid:"1"},{ name:"B",tE:2,tN:10,cE:2,cN:20,pmid:"1"}]` yields zero rows because it only splits on exact `{name:"`; consequence: valid rows with whitespace are invisible.

- Line 22, selector too narrow: input `{name:"A",tE: 1,tN:10,cE:2,cN:20,pmid:"1"}{name:"B",tE:2,tN:10,cE:2,cN:20,pmid:"1"}` drops row A because `tE: 1` does not match `tE:(...)`; consequence: spacing alone can erase a duplicated-control case.

- Line 22, negation/substring match: input `{name:"A",notE:9,tN:10,cE:2,cN:20,pmid:"1"}` is accepted with `tE=9` because `tE:` matches inside `notE:`; consequence: a non-treatment or negated field can be read as treatment events.

- Line 24, selector too narrow: input `{name:"A",tE:1,tN:10,cE:2,cN:20,pmid: "1"}{name:"B",tE:3,tN:11,cE:4,cN:21,pmid: "1"}` misses the repeated PMID because only `pmid:"..."` matches; consequence: signal A can be vacuous under whitespace formatting.

- Line 25, selector window off-by-one/too short: input `{name:"A",` + `"x"*210` + `included:false,tE:1,tN:10,cE:2,cN:20,pmid:"1"}{name:"B",tE:3,tN:10,cE:2,cN:20,pmid:"2"}` treats A as included because `included:false` is after `win[:200]`; consequence: excluded rows can create false shared-control findings.

- Line 60, check can report zero because marker cannot fire: a current directory containing only `A_REVIEW.html` under 100,000 bytes with `{name:"A",tE:1,tN:10,cE:2,cN:20,pmid:"1"}{name:"B",tE:3,tN:10,cE:2,cN:20,pmid:"1"}` is skipped; consequence: a real duplicate can produce `Scanned 0`.

No finding: CRLF/LF text comparison, merged-cell tabulation, zero conflated with absent.
